#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""FS3 v194 - DONE in hangar and support, a wiped hull comes back.

    DONE       The hangar (V) and the support window (S) get the DONE
               button the rearm window has, under the list: the windows
               are so large that little is left outside them to tap
               (Silvio). The longest hangar list (nine Terran hulls) sets
               its rows a little lower so the button still fits.
    Hangar     "NO TERRAN HANGAR HERE" no longer runs into the HULL column.
    Hulls      A damaged capital ship keeps her picture between frames.
               When the browser wipes such pictures (short of graphics
               memory) she builds it again at once instead of after her
               next hit (Silvio: the Hatshepsut's hull gone for seconds).
    3D         Only the last four hulls shown stay on the graphics card.
    Keys       Footers name each window's own key (V, C, R); "or ESC" only
               outside full screen, where the browser takes ESC (Silvio).
               In the support window R now calls the sixth Vasudan row
               instead of reaching for rearm, and the Colossus is G: C
               opens and closes the window, so it never called her. ESC
               that closes a window no longer switches the pause on too.

Needs v193. Edits src/20_render.js, src/40_world.js, src/58_model3d.js,
src/70_ui.js and
the simulations. Run assemble.py afterwards.
"""
